    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="0847" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg835"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.24/926a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-04-01T22:00:00-04:00">April 1, 1943—10 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>383. Your telegram no. 436, March 6, 2 p.m. and your report no. 81 of March
                        6<anchor n="95" xml:id="d802-f1"/> concerning copper sales apparently do not
                    answer question raised in paragraph 1 of Department’s 153, February 11, 11 p.m.
                    The Department is under pressure to institute the control mentioned in this
                    paragraph. Please telegraph as soon as possible whether Chilean Government
                    agrees.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d802-f1" n="95" xml:id="d802-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
